# ossein guest kernel — DEBUG fragment. NOT shipped.
#
# kernel-fragment + in-guest observability. Build it alongside the ship kernel:
#   just kernel-debug          -> build/kernel-arm64.debug
#   OSSEIN_KERNEL=build/kernel-arm64.debug build/ossein run ...
#
# Why this exists: scheduler investigations need in-guest observability (CONFIG_SCHEDSTATS
# for the wakeup counters, CONFIG_DEBUG_FS for /sys/kernel/debug/sched), but the ship kernel
# should never carry debug surface. ossein-kernel takes --kernel-config, so building a
# separate debug kernel costs nothing.
#
# Everything here is deliberately OFF in the ship kernel; see the ship fragment for why.

# The recipe prepends the ship fragment via kernel/merge-fragments.sh, which DROPS every
# ship line for a symbol named below before concatenating. Plain `cat ship debug` does not work:
# it yields a fragment saying both "# CONFIG_KALLSYMS is not set" and "CONFIG_KALLSYMS=y", and
# build.sh's post-olddefconfig drift check asserts every fragment line survived — so it fails,
# correctly. Anything turned on here must therefore be a full override, not an append.

# --- scheduler introspection ---
# nr_wakeups_local/remote/migrate/affine_attempts in /proc/<pid>/sched, and the domain list
# in /proc/schedstat. This is what proved wake_affine() was never being called. The counters sit
# behind DEFINE_STATIC_KEY_FALSE(sched_schedstats) and are OFF at boot: /proc/<pid>/sched shows
# no nr_wakeups lines until you arm it, which reads as a broken config if you don't expect it.
# Arm with `schedstats=enable` on the cmdline, or at runtime (verified, both):
#   echo 1 > /proc/sys/kernel/sched_schedstats     # the debian base image has no sysctl(8)
CONFIG_SCHEDSTATS=y

# --- debugfs ---
# /sys/kernel/debug/sched/{features,domains}. CONFIG_SCHED_DEBUG no longer exists (upstream
# made the sched debugfs unconditional), so DEBUG_FS is the only gate. NOTE: a container's
# /sys is read-only, so mount it from the guest side or run --privileged.
CONFIG_DEBUG_FS=y

# --- symbols in traces ---
# Cut from the ship kernel for a measured ~1ns getpid layout effect; here it is free and it is
# the difference between a readable panic/perf trace and a wall of hex.
CONFIG_KALLSYMS=y
CONFIG_KALLSYMS_ALL=y

# --- slab debugging ---
# Off in ship (it rode in with SLUB_TINY's removal and cost 65KB for nothing). Here it is the
# tool for slab corruption: boot with slub_debug=FZP.
CONFIG_SLUB_DEBUG=y

# --- in-guest perf events + ftrace ---
# VZ exposes no PMU, so hardware events are unavailable either way — but SOFTWARE events
# (context-switches, page-faults, task-clock) and tracepoints work, and `perf record`/
# `perf sched` in-guest would have made both investigations dramatically cheaper.
CONFIG_PERF_EVENTS=y
CONFIG_FTRACE=y
CONFIG_FUNCTION_TRACER=y
CONFIG_DYNAMIC_FTRACE=y
